What´s the role about? 
   We are looking for a Cloud Infrastructure Engineer to join our&nbsp;internal team at the&nbsp;Munich&nbsp;office.&nbsp;You will be working in an internal facing infrastructure team focusing on innovation&nbsp;and supporting builders at Netlight.&nbsp;You will design, build, and operate secure, resilient, and scalable infrastructure on Azure and AWS, and lead Kubernetes initiatives.&nbsp;You will automate wherever possible, improve our internal platforms, and collaborate closely across locations to ensure smooth day-to-day operations.&nbsp;Our Cloud Infrastructure team supports consultants by&nbsp;facilitating access to the latest AI-models to&nbsp;simplify operations, optimize performance, and free up time for what truly matters — delivering value to clients.  &nbsp;  


 &nbsp; 
  With your help, we aim to:  &nbsp;  



 Bring&nbsp;one of our cloud environments&nbsp;Azure up to a professional standard.&nbsp; 




 Restructure our subscription setup and rework permission concepts to improve control and compliance across our tenant.&nbsp; 




 Build new systems to replace legacy components—and own what we build long term.&nbsp; 


 &nbsp; 
 &nbsp;   Your key responsibilities will be to   


 Design, implement, and operate cloud infrastructure on AWS and Azure (networking, identity, security, compute, storage).&nbsp; 




 Set up and manage Kubernetes clusters (EKS), create and maintain Helm charts, and perform operational tasks like debugging applications running in the cluster.&nbsp; 




 Implement Infrastructure as Code with Terraform&nbsp;and cloud CLIs; familiarity with CloudFormation and its limitations (e.g., in Landing Zone Accelerator contexts) is a plus.&nbsp; 




 Build and maintain CI/CD pipelines; GitLab CI experience is a plus.&nbsp; 




 Improve observability (logging, metrics, tracing) and reliability using SRE practices.&nbsp; 




 Drive security, compliance, and cost optimization across multi-cloud environments.&nbsp; 




 Collaborate in cross-functional projects that enhance our tech environment and internal processes.&nbsp; 


   How can you contribute to it?   


 Around 3 years of hands-on cloud operations experience (infrastructure-focused, not just application-level cloud exposure).&nbsp; 



 Strong knowledge of Azure and/or AWS, with openness to work with—and learn—the other cloud.&nbsp; 



 Practical Kubernetes experience, ideally including cluster setup/management, Helm charts, and debugging workloads.&nbsp; 




 Proficiency with Terraform and cloud CLIs; CloudFormation experience is a plus.&nbsp; 




 CI/CD exposure; GitLab CI is a plus.&nbsp; 




 Fluent in English. Fluency in German and/or Swedish is a plus.&nbsp; 




 A team player who is humble, open-minded, flexible, and takes initiative.&nbsp; 




 Self-management, drive, and a high level of technical curiosity; you enjoy engaging with consultants around you.&nbsp; 




 Openness to learn and grow is essential, complemented by sufficient practical experience to contribute from day one.&nbsp; 




 Someone with the ability to set up technical solutions the right way, use sensible technology and do away with legacy systems.&nbsp; 

 &nbsp; 


 Nice to have&nbsp;&nbsp; 



 Certifications such as AWS Solutions Architect Associate or Azure Administrator Associate (or similar).&nbsp; 




 Experience with landing zone patterns (e.g., AWS Landing Zone Accelerator) and enterprise permission models.&nbsp; 




 Experience with security, compliance, or cost optimization in multi-cloud environments. 


